# T13 (changes/model-routing-configurator), NFR-4 Cross-platform.
#
# Windows CI (core.autocrlf=true) converts LF-committed fixtures to CRLF on
# checkout. test/routing.test.js and test/persona-digests.test.js /
# test/agents-doctor*.test.js assert byte-exact fixture content, including
# the deliberate CRLF fixtures (agents-crlf.md, personas/crlf.md) that must
# stay CRLF on every platform. Declaring the whole fixture tree byte-exact
# keeps every fixture's committed line ending intact regardless of checkout
# platform or autocrlf setting.
test/fixtures/** -text

# changes/flow-diagram-animated T1, NFR-3 Cross-platform.
#
# Windows CI (core.autocrlf=true) would check both SVGs out with CRLF.
# test/flow-figure-animated.test.js asserts the committed animated asset is
# byte-identical to animate(static), and animate() writes LF; a CRLF checkout
# of either file makes that comparison fail on the windows-latest legs.
# Declaring both figures byte-exact keeps their committed LF on every platform.
assets/akili-flow.svg -text
assets/akili-flow-animated.svg -text

# changes/impeccable-hardening T1, DD-6 / NFR-3 Cross-platform.
#
# The vendored Impeccable tree is hash-locked in UPSTREAM.md and
# `impeccable.cmd` must stay CRLF (cmd.exe parses by byte offset). Declaring
# the tree byte-exact keeps every committed byte intact on Windows CI.
.claude/skills/impeccable/** -text
